Content: the Dashavatara as commonly listed in the Puranas (Matsya, Kurma, Varaha, Narasimha, Vamana, Parashurama, Rama,
Krishna, the Buddha or Balarama depending on the list, Kalki). "Avatara" (Sanskrit) means descent. The observation that the
sequence moves from water to land and from animal to human is a common modern reading, presented as such.
Everything else (score, foley, paper, all painting) is original and generated in code for this film.
Rendering and tools: the Lemo-Opuscar style library (Watercolor Brush style) and its core/ tools.
